loader: look for drivers where NixOS links them

Before it loads a driver, the loader checks that its file exists in
LD_LIBRARY_PATH, the usual distribution directories or /etc/ld.so.conf.
NixOS has none of those: the system's drivers are in
/run/opengl-driver/lib, on the loader's RUNPATH, where its dlopen would
find them. So every program found no drivers at all unless something
set LD_LIBRARY_PATH. @driverLink@ is replaced with addDriverRunpath's
driverLink at build time.

diff -ruN a/source/loader/linux/driver_discovery_lin.cpp b/source/loader/linux/driver_discovery_lin.cpp
--- a/source/loader/linux/driver_discovery_lin.cpp
+++ b/source/loader/linux/driver_discovery_lin.cpp
@@ -46,6 +46,9 @@
     auto split = splitPaths(ldLibPath);
     paths.insert(paths.end(), split.begin(), split.end());
   }
+  // Where NixOS links the system's drivers, which is on the loader's own
+  // RUNPATH, so the dlopen that follows finds a driver there.
+  paths.push_back("@driverLink@/lib");
 #if defined(ANDROID)
   paths.push_back("/vendor/lib64");
 #else
